      "id": "claim_0579d9f831b74abc83737ceb118ecc04",
      "statement": "write_nested_gitignore and write_nested_gitattributes write their template only when the file is missing and otherwise append only absent lines, adding the settings.local.json line only when git check-ignore --no-index exits exactly 1; they run on setup of an existing nested repository and on every checkpoint, so a consumer's own lines survive and an older repository gains the union-merge rule.",
